---
// Collectibles hub — pre-release framework page (KD-target: "plague tale legacy collectibles").
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import PreReleaseNotice from '../../components/PreReleaseNotice.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import SourcePanel from '../../components/SourcePanel.astro';
import { SOURCES } from '../../data/sources';
import { ASSETS } from '../../data/assets';

const title = 'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy Collectibles Guide — Notebook, Secrets & Locations';
const description =
  'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy collectibles guide covering the notebook, secrets, artifacts, exploration, and what locations remain unconfirmed before launch.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Collectibles', url: '/collectibles/' },
];

// Series-based reference (clearly labelled prequel inference)
const seriesCollectibles = [
  {
    game: 'A Plague Tale: Innocence (2019)',
    types: 'Curiosities, flowers (for Amicia), Hugo’s trinkets, alchemy carts',
    note: 'Collectibles were tied to optional exploration and character moments, not combat.',
  },
  {
    game: 'A Plague Tale: Requiem (2022)',
    types: 'Feathers, flowers, chapter mementos, knives, and "Collectibles" chapter tracking',
    note: 'Requiem added a per-chapter collectible counter and post-chapter cleanup.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="collection" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="container py-10">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />

    <div class="mt-4"><PreReleaseNotice /></div>

    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="section-kicker">Completion</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy collectibles</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-fog">
        Resonance has not launched, so no complete in-game collectible checklist or per-chapter
        location map is published yet. This page records the official exploration clues now and
        will add hands-on locations only after the release build can be played on August 27, 2026.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <MediaFigure {...ASSETS.minoanRuins} />
    </div>

    <section class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>What the Steam page confirms</h2>
      <p>
        The official description mentions Sophia is "guided by the knowledge safeguarded in your
        notebook" and follows "in your crew's footsteps to explore a richly detailed world,
        unravel its secrets." That points to exploration-driven optional content — secrets, notes,
        and lore items — consistent with the series, but no specific collectible categories are
        named on the store page yet.
      </p>

      <h2>Officially named exploration artifacts</h2>
      <p>
        The official <em>Into The Myth</em> developer post gives two concrete examples of the
        island’s historical artifacts: an <strong>orrery</strong>, a device used to predict the
        movement of the stars, and <strong>seal stones depicting people playing with a bull before
        killing it</strong>. They confirm the kind of environmental history the game wants players
        to investigate; they do <strong>not</strong> confirm a collectible category, a count, a
        chapter location, or an achievement requirement.
      </p>
      <p>
        These are real official examples, not a finished “all collectibles” list. The safest
        pre-release answer to “where are the collectibles?” is that the locations have not been
        published. The <a href="/locations/">locations guide</a> covers the confirmed world
        context, while the <a href="/walkthrough/">walkthrough hub</a> will hold verified chapter
        routes after launch.
      </p>

      <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3">
        How collectibles worked in the series
        <StatusBadge status="prequel" size="sm" />
      </h2>
      <p>
        Until launch, the most reliable guide is how Asobo handled collectibles in the two earlier
        games. This is <strong>series-based inference</strong>, not confirmed Resonance content:
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Game</th><th>Collectible types</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {seriesCollectibles.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.game}</td>
              <td>{row.types}</td>
              <td>{row.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Our launch-day plan</h2>
      <p>
        On release day we will publish per-chapter collectible pages with screenshots, map
        markers, and missable warnings, using the same source-tracked approach as the rest of the
        site. Bookmark this page — it becomes the collectibles index the moment the game unlocks.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Chapter-by-chapter location lists with screenshots</li>
        <li>Missable collectible warnings before points of no return</li>
        <li>A completion checklist for 100% and any collectible-linked achievements</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <SourcePanel sources={[SOURCES.steam, SOURCES.steamNews, SOURCES.steamMedia]} />
  </div>
</Layout>
